<title>USA: Coca-Cola Enterprises may issue debt.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola Enterprises may issue debt.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Sept 25 - Coca-Cola Enterprises is expected to price $250 million in debt via Lehman Brothers, syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>The issue consist of a 30-year bond with a put option in the 10th year. Price talk is 33 to 36 basis points over the 10-year U.S. Treasury, sources added.</p>
<p>The issue is rated A3 by Moody's Investors Service Inc and AA-minus by Standard &amp; Poor's.</p>
<p>--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675</p>
</text>
